{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"9HvjjSwxxubIhG6E_sObfQ","review_id":"Jp1tGorSkCidr86PBrI2EA","date":"2017-06-22T16:00:39","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.95090651512146,"text_excerpt":"Mmmm I've come to love po boys during my short stay in NOLA. I tried the fried shrimp with bisque yesterday night at killer po boys for dinner and this place does not disappoint. It's conveniently located on the far end of bourbon street which is nice. I don't have to eat my dinner with crazy loud music and drunk people. The po boy was loaded with juicy pieces of fried shrimp. It came dressed with mayo, tomato and lettuce. I split an 8 inch with my friend and it filled us both up. I loved the bread the sandwich came in. The bread was very soft with enough crunch on the edges. They also served sno balls here which I didn't try but if I have enough time during my stay in NOLA I'll probably ..."},{"business_id":"9HvjjSwxxubIhG6E_sObfQ","review_id":"R003bmVF6lojhWTrynHJFA","date":"2020-01-07T19:48:31","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9504236578941345,"text_excerpt":"If you look at my reviews, I have eaten many places in NOLA. I love to find new places to eat. With that said how did I not try this place sooner? First the ambiance and decor are very unusual and make you seem at home in the bayou. They have 3 sections of seating sort of shotgun style. While we were in there, they were playing some Cuban music. Although they will play anything with a good beat. The staff is super friendly and always check on you to make sure your OK. They will also recommend the best po boys if you unsure what you want. And they will make sure you get it the way you want. Spicy or not. Now the GREAT part. The food. My son who is 11 is very picky. He had a plain cheesebur..."},{"business_id":"9HvjjSwxxubIhG6E_sObfQ","review_id":"V-mWDyBdmzynzYWoQxAP8A","date":"2018-02-18T23:23:15","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9472318291664124,"text_excerpt":"We decided to try Nola's po'boy since they had DaYat Shrimp . Basically we learned a po'boy use to be a poor boy's sandwich. Which was bread, lettuce, mayo & protein. Here we got the fried shrimp which is topped with their gumbo! The norm is also spicy! Have to say I really did enjoy my sandwich!! Yum! Shrimp was fried perfectly and topped with gumbo which is not over powering. You'd barely know it was on there. They have a bun, 8\", or 12\". We split the 8\". Just enough! Cashier was ok. Server was friendly. Booths need some improvement work but it seems the norm for Bourbon St."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"9HvjjSwxxubIhG6E_sObfQ","photo_id":"2Y4b2G0k9RfxlKUVRoQQZQ","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/2Y4b2G0k9RfxlKUVRoQQZQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8884592056274414},{"business_id":"9HvjjSwxxubIhG6E_sObfQ","photo_id":"n94AE6v6WO4sY41A97UzYg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/n94AE6v6WO4sY41A97UzYg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8611184358596802},{"business_id":"9HvjjSwxxubIhG6E_sObfQ","photo_id":"jSTNTCN-Z5LnCkjwR3temQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/jSTNTCN-Z5LnCkjwR3temQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7862130403518677},{"busin